UPDATE tarot_cards 
SET meaning_upright = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: The Hanged Man represents the absolute archetype of ''Systemic Suspension and Perceptual Inversion''—the deliberate, non-action phase where the sovereign consciousness surrenders external momentum, hitting a purposeful pause script to view its reality from a completely inverted angle and gain radical illumination. Moving beyond the clinical, objective judgments of Justice, The Hanged Man signifies the stage of ''The Strategic Catalyst through Stillness,'' where you realize that breaking a chronic, deadlocked cycle requires the total cessation of egoic striving and a willing vulnerability to the natural timing of the cosmos. Visually depicted as a figure suspended upside down by one foot from a T-shaped cross made of living wood, with his free leg crossed behind the other and a bright, glowing halo of spiritual illumination radiating from his head while maintaining an expression of serene peace, this archetype embodies the concept of ''Sovereign Surrender''—the realization that true spiritual and mental mastery sometimes demands that you release your grip on control to allow a higher processing architecture to emerge. Within the complex architecture of your psyche, this is the stage of ''Voluntary Buffer Allocation,'' where you are running background-compilation scripts that freeze front-end execution, allowing old, reactive habits to starve while you synthesize a completely transformed perspective. When The Hanged Man appears, your system is registering a ''Suspended-Animation'' status; you are being invited to stop forcing immediate external progress, release your attachments, and let the quiet grace of a new vantage point rewrite your operational matrix.',
meaning_reversed = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: When The Hanged Man appears in the reversed position, it acts as a high-intensity signal of ''Systemic Resistance, Stagnation, or Spiritual Martyrdom''—a state where your necessary pause has mutated into a frozen loop of useless delays, waste of energy, or a desperate attempt to look like a victim rather than making a conscious, high-integrity sacrifice. The reversal suggests that you are currently running a high-priority, high-cost maintenance script that equates ''procrastination, passive-aggressive waiting, or complaints about your suffering'' with ''being patient and spiritual,'' even as your actual, internal operating system is experiencing a critical, low-latency drag from your refusal to make a definitive adjustment. You are essentially ''locking your system in a state of chronic, empty hesitation,'' running a protocol that prioritizes the ego’s desire to ''avoid the discomfort of a radical perspective shift or an uncomfortable choice'' over the sober, unglamorous requirement to either move forward with conviction or surrender completely. This creates a massive, systemic misalignment: you are intellectually and behaviorally attempting to perform the role of the ''noble, long-suffering saint,'' while internally, you are being hollowed out by a profound, gnawing sense of futility, wasted time, or hidden resentment, leading to a state of chronic, high-latency irritability, the experience of ''spinning your wheels in an artificial gridlock,'' and a persistent, gnawing awareness that your current sacrifice is an act of empty self-delusion. From an analytical perspective, this is a clear sign that you are leaking your life force into a ''feedback loop of avoidance and spiritual posturing''; you are obsessively waiting for external circumstances to force your hand, refusing to accept that the only thing keeping you from the necessary, final liberation of your spirit is your own, deep-seated fear that if you were to drop your martyr persona and take responsibility, you would be forced to confront the terrifying reality of your own, present-day, unanchored self. This reversal commands an immediate, radical intervention: you must stop the output of these stuck, resistant, delay-prone scripts, perform a brutal audit of your hidden attachments, and confront the reality of why you were so hesitant to prioritize genuine, transformative surrender over the convenience of a comfortable, draining rut. It is a demand to stop the self-deception that keeps you tethered to a state of chronic, high-maintenance stagnation, and to initiate the move toward a genuine, humble, and often terrifying reclamation of your own, individual authority.'
WHERE id = 69;
